  "question": {
    "text": "A geostationary satellite orbits around the earth in a circular orbit of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>. Then, the time period of a sky satellite orbiting a few <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math> above the earth&#39;s surface <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> will approximately be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>By Kepler&#39;s law of planetary motion,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&#8733;</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup></math></p><p>Similarly <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&#8733;</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>36000</mn></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>6400</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>6400</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mn>36000</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#62;</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>6400</mn><mn>3600</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>24</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>8</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>45</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math></p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8773;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math></p>"
  }
